# Claude Code Configuration for NUSA Project

# This file configures how Claude Code behaves in this repository
# Learn more: https://docs.claude.ai/claude-code/configuration

# ============================================
# PROJECT-SPECIFIC INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================

## Project Phase: DEVELOPMENT (Product, Design & Implementation)
# We are transitioning from planning to implementation
# CODE should only be written after gathering full context from documentation

## Working Mode
# - Focus on product refinement, feature specification, and wireframing
# - Always use plan mode for any substantial work
# - Present plans for review BEFORE executing
# - Ask clarifying questions rather than making assumptions

## Key Principles
1. **Plan First, Execute Second**
   - For any request involving multiple steps or decisions, ALWAYS enter plan mode
   - Present the plan with options and rationale
   - Wait for approval before proceeding

2. **Structured Thinking**
   - Break down requests into clear phases
   - Identify dependencies and prerequisites
   - Consider multiple approaches and present trade-offs

3. **Design-Focused**
   - Prioritize user experience over technical implementation
   - Think about edge cases and user journeys
   - Validate against the product roadmap principles

4. **Documentation-First**
   - All decisions should be documented in markdown files
   - Keep the product-roadmap.md as the single source of truth
   - Create separate documents for detailed specifications

5. **Git Workflow - User Controls Commits**
   - NEVER commit changes unless user explicitly requests it
   - NEVER push to remote unless user explicitly requests it
   - User will decide when and how to commit/push
   - Only create/modify files when requested
   - User will say "commit" or "commit and push" when ready

6. **Shared-First Code Architecture (MANDATORY)**
   - ALL non-UI code (types, API calls, validation, utils, constants) MUST live in `packages/shared/`
   - `apps/mobile/` and `apps/web/` MUST import from `@nusa/shared` — NEVER redefine locally
   - `packages/shared/` MUST NOT import from `react-native`, `expo-*`, or `next`
   - If the same type/function/constant exists in more than one place, it belongs in `packages/shared/`
   - Always read `docs/code-sharing-guide.md` and `docs/monorepo-structure.md` before implementing

## Implementation Workflow (CRITICAL)

When implementing features, ALWAYS follow this sequence:

1. **Context Gathering** (MANDATORY before coding)
   - Read feature specification: `docs/features/[feature-name].md` (if exists)
   - Read user journey: `docs/user-journeys/[category]/[number]-[journey-name].md`
   - Read wireframes: `docs/wireframes/[screen-name].md`
   - Read design system: `docs/wireframes/00-design-system-foundation.md`
   - Read code sharing guide: `docs/code-sharing-guide.md`
   - Read monorepo structure: `docs/monorepo-structure.md`

2. **Platform & Sharing Analysis** (MANDATORY before planning)
   - Determine target platforms: Mobile, Web, or Both (default: Both)
   - For each code unit, decide: `packages/shared/` or `apps/{platform}/`?
   - List what goes in `packages/shared/` FIRST
   - Check existing `packages/shared/src/index.ts` exports to avoid duplication

3. **Planning** (Use EnterPlanMode)
   - Map documentation to code structure
   - Identify all components needed
   - Define file structure with shared package as foundation
   - Create validation checklist

4. **Implementation** (Only after approval — SHARED LAYER FIRST)
   - Shared types in `packages/shared/src/types/`
   - Shared validation in `packages/shared/src/validation/`
   - Shared API functions in `packages/shared/src/api/` (dependency injection pattern)
   - Shared utils/constants in `packages/shared/src/utils/` and `constants/`
   - Update `packages/shared/src/index.ts` exports
   - Mobile UI: screens, components, navigation importing from `@nusa/shared`
   - Web UI: pages, components importing from `@nusa/shared`
   - Handle all error cases from documentation

5. **Validation** (Before marking complete)
   - Verify implementation matches wireframes pixel-perfect
   - Test all interactive states (default, pressed, disabled, error, loading)
   - Verify all validation rules from wireframes
   - Test all edge cases from user journey
   - Run `/shared-first-check` to verify no duplicated types/logic
   - Demo to user and iterate

**Use `/implement-feature [feature-name]` skill for guided implementation.**

## File Organization
- `product-roadmap.md` - Master roadmap (single source of truth)
- `docs/features/` - Detailed feature specifications
- `docs/wireframes/` - Wireframe descriptions and references
- `docs/user-journeys/` - User flow documentation
- `docs/decisions/` - Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)
- `docs/implementation/` - Implementation notes and deviations

## Communication Style
- Ask questions when requirements are unclear
- Present options with pros/cons rather than making unilateral decisions
- Use visual formatting (tables, diagrams, checklists) for clarity
- Summarize complex topics before diving into details
